      "content": "| Feature             | ETFs (Exchange-Traded Funds)                 | Mutual Funds               |\n|---------------------|------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|\n| Liquidity           | High - traded throughout the day like stocks  | Lower - trades occur at the end of the trading day |\n| Management Style    | Passive - often track an index                  | Active - managed by fund managers to outperform the market |\n\nETFs offer greater liquidity as they're traded throughout the day, making them easier to buy and sell at market value. They typically have a passive management style, as they're designed to match the performance of an index, with lower turnover rates. Mutual funds, on the other hand, have lower liquidity since trades are only at the end of the day and they often incur a price difference due to the buying and selling process. Their management style is generally more active, as fund managers actively select securities in an attempt to outperform the market.",
